  "stdout": "reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Ammonium_Molybdate_Tetrahydrate.after.yaml:2:preferred_term: ammonium molybdate tetrahydrate\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Ammonium_Molybdate_Tetrahydrate.after.yaml:5:  ontology_label: hexaammonium heptamolybdate tetrahydrate\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Ammonium_Molybdate_Tetrahydrate.after.yaml:14:    notes: Parent class identified via stem-substring; matched_via='ammonium molybdate tetrahydrate'\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Ammonium_Molybdate_Tetrahydrate.after.yaml:17:    notes: 'mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning* than CHEBI:91249 (''ammonium molybdate'') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 ''hydrate'', never under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record''s own identifier are unchanged.'\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Ammonium_Molybdate_Tetrahydrate.after.yaml:20:    notes: 'identifier cas:12054-85-2 -> CHEBI:86244; ontology CHEBI:91249 (''ammonium molybdate'') -> CHEBI:86244 (''hexaammonium heptamolybdate tetrahydrate''); mapping_quality CLOSE_MATCH -> SYNONYM_MATCH. The record (H32Mo7N6O28, CAS 12054-85-2) is the heptamolybdate; CHEBI:91249 ''ammonium molybdate'' is the diammonium orthomolybdate (2H4N.MoO4, one Mo), a different polyanion, not the anhydrous parent of this hydrate. ChEBI has the substance: CHEBI:86244 ''hexaammonium heptamolybdate tetrahydrate'' (4H2O.6H4N.Mo7O24) carries the related synonym ''ammonium molybdate tetrahydrate'', the record''s exact label, on no other term. Section 3 step 1 with a unique synonym: SYNONYM_MATCH. The CAS stays on its registry row.'\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Ammonium_Molybdate_Tetrahydrate.after.yaml:22:    source: all_unmatched_20261107 worker04 primary proposal heptamolybdate-tetrahydrate\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Ammonium_Molybdate_Tetrahydrate.after.yaml:23:    notes: The raw source(NH4)6Mo7O24 x4H2O, ingredient120 CAS12054-85-2 and mass1235.86 identify hexaammonium heptamolybdate tetrahydrate86244. Diammonium orthomolybdate91249 has one Mo and two ammoniums and is not its parent. The current wrong owner already rejects the tetrahydrate strings but still resolves the anhydrous heptamolybdate formula; reject that residual polyanion alias and link the source to the existing correct tetrahydrate owner. OLS86244's prose says heptahydrate in error; its name/formula/mass and source CAS all specify four waters. Evidence and exact frozen scope are recorded in reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/fragments/chemistry-decisions.json. This proposed delta does not approve complete owner/export payload or remove inherited holds.\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Ammonium_Molybdate_Tetrahydrate.after.yaml:28:- synonym_text: (NH4)6Mo7O4\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Ammonium_Molybdate_Tetrahydrate.after.yaml:31:- synonym_text: (NH4)6Mo7O4 x 24 H2O\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Ammonium_Molybdate_Tetrahydrate.after.yaml:43:- synonym_text: (NH4)Mo7O24·4H2O\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Ammonium_Molybdate_Tetrahydrate.after.yaml:52:- synonym_text: ammonium heptamolybdate tetrahydrate\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Ammonium_Molybdate_Tetrahydrate.after.yaml:55:- synonym_text: ammonium paramolybdate tetrahydrate\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Ammonium_Molybdate_Tetrahydrate.after.yaml:58:- synonym_text: (NH4)6Mo7O24 x 4 H2O\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Ammonium_Molybdate_Tetrahydrate.after.yaml:80:  changes: molecular_formula=H32Mo7N6O28; smiles=N.N.N.N.N.N.O.O.O.O.O[Mo](=O)(=O)O.O[Mo](=O)(=O)O.; inchi=InChI=1S/7Mo.6H3N.10H2O.18O/h;;;;;;;6*1H3;10*1H2;;\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Ammonium_Molybdate_Tetrahydrate.after.yaml:112:  changes: 'Recovered 8 surface form(s) that the published SSSOM `other` carried but no curated record did, so a rebuild would have dropped them from KGX: ''(NH4)6Mo7O4''; ''(NH4)6Mo7O4 x 24 H2O''; ''(NH4)6MoO24·4H2O''; ''(NH4)6MoO7O24''; ''(NH4)6MoO7O24 x 4 H2O''; ''(NH4)Mo7O24·4H2O''; ''(NH4)MoO7O24''; ''(NH4)MoO7O24 x 4 H2O''. Tokens already present on the kg-microbe ontology node were left out as redundant (#520).'\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Ammonium_Molybdate_Tetrahydrate.after.yaml:117:  changes: 'Marked hidden hydrate synonym(s) as REJECTED_LABEL so this record no longer resolves sibling hydrate identities (#251): ''(NH4)6Mo7O4 x 24 H2O''.'\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Ammonium_Molybdate_Tetrahydrate.after.yaml:129:  changes: 'identifier cas:12054-85-2 -> CHEBI:86244; ontology CHEBI:91249 (''ammonium molybdate'') -> CHEBI:86244 (''hexaammonium heptamolybdate tetrahydrate''); mapping_quality CLOSE_MATCH -> SYNONYM_MATCH. The record (H32Mo7N6O28, CAS 12054-85-2) is the heptamolybdate; CHEBI:91249 ''ammonium molybdate'' is the diammonium orthomolybdate (2H4N.MoO4, one Mo), a different polyanion, not the anhydrous parent of this hydrate. ChEBI has the substance: CHEBI:86244 ''hexaammonium heptamolybdate tetrahydrate'' (4H2O.6H4N.Mo7O24) carries the related synonym ''ammonium molybdate tetrahydrate'', the record''s exact label, on no other term. Section 3 step 1 with a unique synonym: SYNONYM_MATCH. The CAS stays on its registry row. (#312) Synonyms added: ammonium heptamolybdate tetrahydrate, am